{
  "name": "436. A sync image response says when its links expire (image link expiry)",
  "description": "TXE-7051, contract C9. Local fixture regression, no live provider calls: run with providerErrorFixture=1 against the gateway of tests/e2e/api/provider_config/provider-error-fixture.config.json, with tests/e2e/api/runners/provider-error-fixture.mjs as the only upstream. Before the change no sync image response carried an expiry, so a caller that downloads the links had no deadline to read. Now a response with at least one link, from a provider that documents a fixed link lifetime (schemas.ImageLinkLifetimes: BytePlus Seedream, MiniMax and Alibaba DashScope 24 hours, Tencent TokenHub 12 hours), carries expires_at = created + that lifetime, written in one place for every such provider. The rows cover both routes the change reaches: MiniMax generation (a link back carries expires_at counted from the time the answer was read, because MiniMax reports no creation time; bytes back carry none), and BytePlus Seedream generation and edit (expires_at counted from the created Seedream reports). Providers with no documented lifetime are pinned by Go tests.",
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "minimax/image-01 /v1/images/generations with a link back: expires_at is created plus the 24 hours MiniMax documents (image link expiry)",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "prerequest",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "if (pm.variables.get('providerErrorFixture') !== '1') {",
              "  pm.execution.skipRequest();",
              "}"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "var text = pm.response.text();",
              "var body = pm.response.json();",
              "pm.test('the client gets 200 with one link', function () {",
              "  pm.expect(pm.response.code, text).to.equal(200);",
              "  pm.expect(body.data, text).to.be.an('array').with.length(1);",
              "  pm.expect(body.data[0].url, text).to.match(/^https:\\/\\//);",
              "});",
              "pm.test('expires_at is created + 86400', function () {",
              "  pm.expect(body.created, text).to.be.a('number').above(0);",
              "  pm.expect(body.expires_at, text).to.equal(body.created + 86400);",
              "});"
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "Content-Type",
            "value": "application/json"
          }
        ],
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\"model\":\"minimax/image-01\",\"prompt\":\"a lighthouse at dusk\",\"n\":1}"
        },
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/v1/images/generations",
          "host": [
            "{{baseUrl}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "v1",
            "images",
            "generations"
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    {
